add(R, passage(P, PCPT163, `위 글을 읽고 나눈 대화 중, 글의 내용과 일치하지 않는 것은?`), '2', ['A: I am surprised to learn that there are several pacers helping runners in the race. / B: Me, too. Now I can understand why there are so many people running at the race.', 'A: Runners usually lead pacers to finish the race as quickly as possible. / B: Yes, pacers get a lot of help from runners during a race.', 'A: I learned that there is a place on the side of the race track and it is called a pit. / B: Oh, yeah. Drivers stop there several times.', 'A: What is the main job of the pit crew? / B: Their job is to check the car and change the tires.', 'A: What do you think is important for car racing? / B: Since almost 20 members have to work together in a short time, the perfect harmony seems important.']);
const PIT180 = `You may only see the car and the driver during most car races, but there is a team behind the driver. This team is called a pit crew. A pit is a place on the side of the race track, and drivers stop there several times ⓐ<u>for</u> a race. The main job of the pit crew is to check the car and change the tires. Changing the tires ⓑ<u>are</u> especially important because the tires ⓒ<u>wearing out</u> easily in a high speed race.\nA pit stop can be as short as 2 seconds, and there are ⓓ<u>as much as</u> 20 members on a crew. Therefore, the pit crew has to work in perfect harmony. The driver may get all the attention, but as people say, "Races ⓔ<u>win</u> in the pits."`;
