const INPC184 = `In sports, only the players get a trophy or medal, but they don't win on their own. There are people who help the players. These people are often hidden and don't get attention. However, they are ⓐ<u>as important as the players</u>. Here is an example.\nPacers run with other runners and lead them in a marathon. ⓑ<u>Pacers are experienced runners, and their job is to help other runners managing their race better</u>. There can be several pacers in a race.\nⓒ<u>Each pacer run at different speeds and finish the race in different times</u>. ⓓ<u>Pacers usually have flags or balloons that show their finish time</u>.\nⓔ<u>Runners can choose a pacer depend on their target finish time</u>. For example, if a runner wants to finish the race in four hours, the runner will follow the four-hour pacer. ⓕ<u>Since the pacer keeps track of the time, the runner can achieve his or her goal of finishing the marathon in a particular time more easily</u>. (A)<u>요컨대, 페이서들은 달리기는 하지만 그들이 우승을 하기 위해 달리는 것은 아니다</u>. They run for others.`;
add(R, passage(P, INPC184, `위 글의 밑줄 친 ⓐ~ⓕ 중 어법상 알맞은 것의 개수는?`), '2', ['2개', '3개', '4개', '5개', '6개']);
add(R, passage(P, INPC184, `위 글의 밑줄 친 (A)의 우리말과 같은 뜻이 되도록 <보기>에 주어진 단어를 알맞게 배열하시오.${FULL}\n\n<보기> to / but / run / they / pacers / in / don't / short / win / run\n\n→ ______________________`), "In short, pacers run but they don't run to win.", null);
add(R, passage(P, INPC184, `위 글의 제목으로 알맞은 것은?`), '4', ['Helpful Tips for Runners', 'The Main Role of Flags in Sports', 'Challenges of Running a Marathon Alone', 'People Who Help Runners in a Marathon', 'Speed: The Most Important Thing to Win a Marathon']);
add(R, passage(P, INPC184, `위 글을 읽고 나눈 대화 중 글의 내용을 바르게 이해한 것을 두 개 고르면? (정답 2개)`), '3, 5', ['A: What do pacers run for? / B: They run for a trophy or medal.', "A: What do the pacers' flags or balloons show? / B: Flags or balloons show the finish line.", 'A: Do players get a trophy or medal on their own? / B: No, there are people who help the players.', 'A: How do runners choose a pacer in a marathon? / B: Each runner is paired with one pacer depending on his or her age and experience.', "A: Why is it that pacers are as important as the runners? / B: It's because runners can achieve their goal more easily with the help of pacers."]);
