add(R, passage(P, PIT, `위 글을 읽고 다음 질문에 답할 때, 빈칸에 들어갈 알맞은 말을 본문에서 찾아 10단어로 쓰시오.\n\nQ. Why is changing tires important in a car race?\n\n→ It is important because ______________________.`), 'the tires wear out easily in a high speed race', null);
add(R, `다음 글에 이어질 내용으로 알맞은 것은?\n\n${INTRO}`, '3', ['how to build team spirit', 'the main goal of a sport player', 'examples of hidden people in sports', 'players doing their best to win a game', 'examples of people getting most attention in a sport']);
add(R, `다음 글의 내용과 일치하는 것은?\n\nCheerleaders in Football Games\nAlthough people usually don't think that cheerleaders are a part of a football team, they play an important role in a football game. By cheering at a game, they create team spirit. They also encourage their team and fans. To do their job well, cheerleaders need to be fit and strong. They also need to be good at jumping and dancing. Most of all, they need to work as hard as the players.`, '2', ['Cheerleaders are not a part of a football team.', 'Health and strength are needed to be a good cheerleader.', 'It is hard for cheerleaders to encourage their team and fans in games.', 'Football players have to work harder than cheerleaders all the time.', 'Many people know that cheerleaders are very important in a football game.']);

