const PTSH188 = `Pit Crews in Car Racing\n(A) You may only see the car and the driver during most car races, but there is a team behind the driver. This team is called a pit crew. A pit is a place on the side of the race track, and drivers stop there several times during a race. (B) Changing the tires is especially important because the tires wear out easily in a high speed race. (C)\nA pit stop can be as short as 2 seconds, and there are as many as 20 members on a crew. (D) Therefore, the pit crew has to work in perfect harmony. The driver may get all the attention, but as people say, "Races are won in the pits." (E)\n\nSherpas in Mountain Climbing\nThe word Sherpa comes from the Sherpa tribe, which lives in the eastern part of Nepal. Sherpas have good climbing skills and know their way around the mountains well. They also have little difficulty breathing high up in the mountains. Therefore, mountain climbers ⓐ<u>자신들이 에베레스트 산을 등반하는 것을 돕는 셰르파를 고용하기 시작했다</u>.\nSherpas lead mountain climbers to the top of the mountain. They support climbers in many ways. For example, they put up tents and carry climbers' bags. Sherpas are often called the invisible people of Mount Everest because people often see a picture of only the climbers at the top of the mountain.`;
add(R, passage(P, PTSH188, `위 글의 (A)~(E) 중 주어진 문장이 들어갈 알맞은 곳은?\n\nThe main job of the pit crew is to check the car and change the tires.`), '2', ABCDE);
add(R, passage(P, PTSH188, `위 글의 밑줄 친 ⓐ의 우리말과 같은 뜻이 되도록 <보기>의 단어 및 표현을 알맞게 배열할 때, 일곱 번째로 오는 것은?\n\n<보기> to / started / them / climb / to / help / Sherpas / Mount Everest / hire`), '1', ['them', 'hire', 'help', 'climb', 'Sherpas']);
add(R, passage(P, PTSH188, `위 글을 읽고 답할 수 없는 것은?`), '4', ['In car racing, what is a pit?', 'Where does the word Sherpa come from?', 'Why is changing the tires important in a car race?', 'How much money do climbers pay for hiring Sherpas?', 'Why are Sherpas called the invisible people of Mount Everest?']);
add(R, `다음 글의 밑줄 친 ⓐ~ⓔ 중, 흐름상 어색한 것은?\n\nPacers run with other runners and lead them in a marathon. Pacers are experienced runners, and their job is to help other runners manage their race better. There can be several pacers in a race.\nEach pacer runs at different speeds and finishes the race in different times. Pacers usually have flags or balloons showing their finish time.\nⓐ<u>Runners can choose a pacer depending on their target finish time</u>. ⓑ<u>For example, if a runner wants to finish the race in four hours, the runner will follow the four-hour pacer</u>. ⓒ<u>Since the pacer keeps track of the time, the runner can achieve his or her goal of finishing the marathon in a particular time more easily</u>. ⓓ<u>In short, pacers run but they don't run to win</u>. ⓔ<u>They run for themselves</u>.`, '5', CIRCLE);
const SH197 = `The word Sherpa comes from the Sherpa tribe ⓐ<u>living</u> in the eastern part of Nepal. (A) Sherpas have good climbing skills and know their way around the mountains well. (B) They also have ⓑ<u>little</u> difficulty breathing high up in the mountains. (C) Therefore, mountain climbers started to hire Sherpas to help them ⓒ<u>climbed</u> Mount Everest. (D) Sherpas lead mountain climbers to the top of the mountain. (E) For example, they put up tents and ⓓ<u>carry</u> climbers' bags. Sherpas are often called the invisible people of Mount Everest ⓔ<u>as</u> people often see a picture of only the climbers at the top of the mountain.`;
add(R, passage(P, SH197, `위 글의 밑줄 친 ⓐ~ⓔ 중, 어법상 어색한 것은?`), '3', CIRCLE);
add(R, passage(P, SH197, `위 글의 (A)~(E) 중, 주어진 문장이 들어갈 알맞은 곳은?\n\nThey support climbers in many ways.`), '5', ABCDE);
add(R, passage(P, SH197, `위 글에 언급된 Sherpa에 대한 설명으로 알맞지 않은 것은?`), '4', ['They are good at climbing mountains.', 'They can show climbers the way to the top of Mt. Everest.', 'They support mountain climbers by setting up tents.', 'They usually suffer from breathing problems in the high mountains.', 'They are not seen in a picture of the climbers at the summit of the mountain.']);
add(R, passage(P, SHERPA.replace('Sherpas in Mountain Climbing\n', ''), `위 글에 언급된 셰르파의 장점 세 가지를 찾아 우리말로 서술하시오. (본문에 언급된 순서대로 적을 것)\n\n(1) ______________________\n(2) ______________________\n(3) ______________________`), '훌륭한 등산 기술을 가지고 있다. / 산의 지리에 밝다. / 산의 높은 곳에서 호흡하는 데 어려움이 없다.', null, { subParts: sp(['훌륭한 등산 기술을 가지고 있다.', '산의 지리에 밝다.', '산의 높은 곳에서 호흡하는 데 어려움이 없다.']) });
add(R, passage(P, PIT, `위 글의 내용과 일치하는 것은?`), '1', ['There is a team called a pit crew behind the driver in a car race.', "The pit crew doesn't need to work together.", 'Drivers stop in the pit only once during a race.', 'The pit crew wants to get all the attention.', 'Races are won only by the driver.']);
add(R, `다음 글의 목적으로 알맞은 것은?\n\nDo you like riding a bike? Then, I suggest you join our club, Fun Wheels. We ride bikes once a week, on Saturdays. We ride along the river or in parks. It's fun to ride bikes together. Riding bikes will make you feel happy and joyful.`, '1', ['자전거 동아리 가입을 제안하려고', '자전거의 바퀴에 대해 설명하려고', '자전거를 탈 때 필요한 사항을 알려 주려고', '주중에 할 수 있는 유용한 활동을 소개하려고', '강과 공원에서 지켜야 하는 규칙을 알려 주려고']);

