const SH216 = `(A) The word Sherpa comes from the Sherpa tribe, which lives in the eastern part of Nepal. (B) Sherpas have good climbing skills and know their way around the mountains well. They also have little difficulty breathing high up in the mountains. (C) Since then, Sherpas have led mountain climbers to the top of the mountain. They support climbers in many ways. (D) For example, they put up tents and carry climbers' bags. (E) Sherpas are often called the invisible people of Mount Everest because ⓐ______________________________.`;
add(R, passage(P, SH216, `위 글의 (A)~(E) 중, 주어진 문장이 들어갈 알맞은 곳은?\n\nTherefore, mountain climbers started to hire Sherpas to help them climb Mount Everest.`), '3', ABCDE);
add(R, passage(P, SH216, `위 글을 읽고 나눈 대화의 빈칸에 들어갈 알맞은 질문을 고르면?\n\nA: ______________________________\nB: They put up tents and carry climbers' bags.`), '1', ['How do Sherpas usually support climbers?', 'Where does the word Sherpa come from?', 'What is the highest mountain in the world?', 'How much money do Sherpas get when they help climbers?', 'Why do the climbers have difficulty in breathing high up in the mountains?']);
add(R, passage(P, `${INTRO}\n${PACER.replace('Pacers in a Marathon\n', '')}`, `위 글의 제목으로 가장 알맞은 것을 고르시오.\n\nWhat is the best title of the passage above?`), '3', ["How to Manage One's Running Time", 'Methods of Becoming a Great Runner', 'Hidden but Important People in Sports', 'Examples of the Best Pacers in the World', 'Relationship between Runners and Players']);
add(R, `다음 글의 내용과 일치하지 않는 것은?\n\nThe word caddie comes from the French word le cadet, meaning "the boy." In Europe in the 18th century, caddies carried water to houses. The first mention of caddies carrying golf clubs is in 1857. Now, caddies are not boys, and both men and women can be caddies.\nThe caddie supports the golf player in many ways. The caddie is in charge of carrying the golf player's bag and cleaning the golf balls. The caddie also has to find where the golf ball is for the player after the player hits it. The caddie must know the golf course well so he or she can give advice to the player. Caddies make a difference between winning and losing in a game.`, '2', ['The word caddie originates from the French word.', 'Caddies originally carried water for golfers.', 'Now, caddies can be both men and women.', 'The caddie helps the golf player by giving the player advice.', 'The caddie is responsible for finding the golf ball for the player.']);

